# An Interdisciplinary Bibliography for Computers and the Humanities Courses.

**Authors:** Ehrlich, Heyward

## Abstract
Presents an annotated bibliography of works related to the subject of computers and the humanities. Groups items into textbooks and overviews; introductions; human and computer languages; literary and linguistic analysis; artificial intelligence and robotics; social issue debates; computers' image in fiction; anthologies; writing and the classroom; science, technology, and society; and journals, newsletters research, and reference. (SG)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ449348

